  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0440\" contains six tables, each representing a different entity or concept. The tables are:\n1. Device: This table stores information about the devices in the system, including their creation time, department, device ID, device image, device model, group, IP address, person in charge, product name, QR code, type, update time, and usage location. The device ID is the primary key, and the table has no foreign keys.\n2. User: This table stores information about the users in the system, including their account status, contact information, name, role, and user ID. The user ID is the primary key, and the table has no foreign keys.\n3. Device_Status: This table stores information about the status of the devices in the system, including their current status, last update time, remarks, and device ID. The device ID is the primary key, and the table has a foreign key referencing the Device table.\n4. Device_Maintenance: This table stores information about the maintenance records of the devices in the system, including the device ID, maintenance content, maintenance person ID, maintenance result, maintenance time, remarks, user satisfaction, and primary key (device ID, maintenance person ID, maintenance time). The device ID and maintenance person ID are foreign keys referencing the Device and User tables, respectively.\n5. Device_Repair_Request: This table stores information about the repair requests for the devices in the system, including the device ID, handling personnel, handling status, handling time, remarks, request content, request time, and requester ID. The device ID and requester ID are foreign keys referencing the Device and User tables, respectively.\n6. Device_Inventory: This table stores information about the inventory of the devices in the system, including the device ID, device location, inventory person ID, and inventory time. The device ID and inventory person ID are foreign keys referencing the Device and User tables, respectively.\nIn summary, the schema \"rschema_0440\" is a comprehensive database that stores information about devices, users, device status, maintenance records, repair requests, and inventory in a relational database management system. The schema is designed to ensure data consistency and integrity across the different tables, with foreign keys and primary keys used to enforce referential and entity integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Device Management System Requirements: This is a device management system. In terms of device management, the system supports the input of device information via a mobile application, including product name, device model, person in charge, group, type, usage location, department, IP address, and device images. A unique QR code is generated for each device, enabling a one-device-one-code system, and records the creation and update times of each device. The system also supports the printing and pasting of QR code labels. In terms of user management, the system maintains each user’s basic information, including a unique user ID, name, role, contact information, and account status. For device inventory management, the system supports exporting in-use device information, including device ID, inventory person ID, inventory time, and device location. In terms of device maintenance, staff can submit maintenance requests, including device ID, requester ID, maintenance time, maintenance content, handling status, handling personnel, handling time, and remarks. After submitting a maintenance request, the system assigns maintenance personnel to handle it and records the maintenance details, including device ID, maintenance personnel ID, maintenance time, maintenance content, maintenance results, user satisfaction, and remarks. The system also regularly updates and records the status information for each device, including current status, last update time, and remarks, to ensure the accuracy and efficiency of device management.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0440.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0440\nCREATE TABLE `device` (\n  `device_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `device_image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `device_model` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `device_group` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `qr_code` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `device_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `usage_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `account_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_status` (\n  `device_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `current_status` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_status_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`device_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_maintenance` (\n  `device_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_person_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `maintenance_result` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_satisfaction` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`, `maintenance_person_id`, `maintenance_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`device_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`maintenance_person_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_repair_request` (\n  `device_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `requester_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `handling_personnel` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `handling_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `handling_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`, `requester_id`, `request_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_repair_request_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`device_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_repair_request_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`requester_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_inventory` (\n  `device_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_person_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `device_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`, `inventory_person_id`, `inventory_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`device_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_inventory_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`inventory_person_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
